        "original_id": "1df41dad-e4d1-5342-bd6c-fede208fe091",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: D. J. Caruso, Christopher Landon, Carl Ellsworth, Shia LaBeouf, David Morse, Sarah Roemer, Carrie-Anne Moss, Michael Landon\n- Works: Disturbia, Even Stevens, Paranormal Activity films\n- Organizations: Disney Channel\n- Roles: actor, performance artist, filmmaker, film director, producer, screenwriter\n\nFacts:\n- Disturbia is a 2007 American horror thriller film directed by D. J. Caruso, written by Christopher Landon and Carl Ellsworth, and starring Shia LaBeouf, David Morse, Sarah Roemer, and Carrie-Anne Moss.\n- Shia LaBeouf was born on June 11, 1986, and is an American actor, performance artist, and filmmaker.\n- Christopher Beau Landon was born on February 27, 1975, and is an American film director, producer, and screenwriter.\n- In 2001, Shia LaBeouf received a Young Artist Award nomination for playing Louis Stevens in the Disney Channel series Even Stevens.\n- In 2003, Shia LaBeouf won a Daytime Emmy Award for his role as Louis Stevens in Even Stevens.\n- Christopher Landon is best known as the writer of the 2007 film Disturbia, the last three Paranormal Activity films, and as the son of late actor Michael Landon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
